LeafAnvil Dual License (Personal / Private Testing & Commercial Server Runtime)
===============================================================================

The LeafAnvil runtime plugin and mod source tree and compiled distribution
(`LeafAnvil-<version>.jar` and `net.leaf.anvil.*` under `resource/LeafAnvil/`,
except for the MIT-licensed components listed in Track 3 below) are
dual-licensed under your choice of:

  - Track 1 (Free Personal Use, Research & Private Testing —
    `PolyForm-Noncommercial-1.0.0`): You may freely inspect, modify, compile
    from source (`https://github.com/LeafCraftDev/LeafAnvil`), and run the
    Software for personal singleplayer worlds, non-commercial private servers
    with friends, local evaluation, CI/benchmarking, security auditing,
    academic research, and noncommercial organizations under the PolyForm
    Noncommercial License 1.0.0 set out in Part I below.

  - Track 2 (Commercial Server & Network Runtime —
    `LicenseRef-LeafCraft-Commercial`): Operating the Software on a
    commercially monetized Minecraft server, proxy network, or hosted game
    service requires a valid commercial license purchased from an authorized
    LeafCraft storefront (such as BuiltByBit, Polymart, SpigotMC Premium, or a
    direct LeafCraft agreement) under the LeafCraft Commercial Software License
    set out in Part II below.

  - Track 3 (Open `.lca` Format, `anvil-api`, `LeafAnvil-Net` & `lca-format` —
    `MIT` Carve-Out):
    1. World Data Ownership: Users retain 100% ownership and unrestricted
       control over all world save files (`.lca`, `.mca`, `.linear`, and
       backups) created, converted, compacted, or repaired by the Software.
    2. Permissive MIT Components (`LICENSE-MIT`): The `.lca` (LeafCraft Anvil)
       binary format Interface Control Document (`api/anvil-api/docs/ICD.md`,
       bundled at `docs/ICD.md`, `LCA-ICD-1.0`), the `io.github.dailystruggle.anvil`
       codec library (`api/anvil-api`), the standalone wire-streaming companion
       mod/plugin (`:resource:LeafAnvil:leafanvil-net`, `LeafAnvil-Net-<version>.jar`),
       and the pure-Rust `.lca` crate (`resource/LeafAnvil/rust/lca-format`) are
       licensed separately under the MIT License (`LICENSE-MIT`), and NeoForge
       carrier adapters in `platforms/neoforge/` remain under `GPL-3.0-or-later`
       per their `neoforge.mods.toml`. Any developer, server fork, world
       generator, map renderer, or external tool may freely inspect, implement,
       bundle, or commercially use those MIT components without restriction.

